  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes around 30 minutes."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Yakisoba"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "is stir-fried wheat noodles with pork, cabbage, and a tangy sauce built around"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worcestershire sauce"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". It is finished with"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "bonito flakes"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "and Japanese mayonnaise. It is a fast, filling weeknight meal cooked in a single pan."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Get the wok very hot before anything goes in. The noodles need high heat to fry and colour, not steam and clump. Add each ingredient in stages rather than all at once. Crowding the wok drops the temperature and turns everything soggy. The pork should be cooked and lightly coloured before the vegetables go in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
